here rather than in the small print because a term of that kind should be
read before it applies rather than after. Section 10 states it in full.

1. DEFINITIONS

1.1 "Koi Ayame" means the individual who created and publishes the
Project.

1.2 "Maintainer" means Koi Ayame, or any successor expressly designated
in writing by Koi Ayame or by a previously designated Maintainer.

1.3 "Copyright Holder" means Koi Ayame and any other person or entity
that owns copyright in material distributed under this license.

1.4 "Project" means the Koi-DOS project maintained or designated by the
Maintainer. The Project is not a separate legal person, and references to
the Project mean the Maintainer acting in relation to it.

1.5 "Software" means only material that is identified as covered by this
license by one or more of the following methods:

(a) the material contains a copyright or KNCL notice;

(b) the material is accompanied by this license;

(c) the material is listed as covered in an official LICENSE-MANIFEST
    file;

(d) the material is located in a source repository, release archive, or
    package directory expressly marked as KNCL-covered; or

(e) official distribution metadata identifies the material as covered by
    KNCL.

Where an official LICENSE-MANIFEST accompanies a distribution, that
manifest is authoritative for the material in that distribution.

Material is not covered by this license merely because it is distributed
in the same repository, archive, disk image, package, or download as
Koi-DOS.

Material identified as subject to another license is governed by that
other license and is not governed by KNCL.

1.6 "Modified Software" means Software, or a copy of Software, in which
one or more covered files have been edited, translated, rearranged,
combined with changes, or otherwise modified, including any version that
constitutes a derivative work under applicable copyright law.

A work is Modified Software only to the extent that it contains or is
based on covered Software. Independent material remains governed by its
own applicable license.

1.7 "Program for Koi-DOS" means an independent program designed to run
on Koi-DOS that does not include, modify, copy, or distribute covered
implementation code from the Software other than Redistributable SDK
Components.

1.8 "Interface Component" means a header, declaration, ABI definition,
system-call definition, protocol definition, file-format definition, or
other material expressly marked by the Maintainer as interface-only.

1.9 "Redistributable SDK Component" means material expressly identified
by the Maintainer as permitted for inclusion in, linking into, and
redistribution alongside Programs for Koi-DOS.

Material may be identified as both an Interface Component and a
Redistributable SDK Component. The two identifications grant different
permissions - one to reimplement an interface, one to redistribute an
implementation - and are cumulative rather than alternatives.

Neither identification changes which license covers the material itself.
A Redistributable SDK Component remains Software, and modifying it as
part of Koi-DOS is governed by this license like anything else; what the
identification adds is permission to carry it inside a Program for
Koi-DOS.

1.10 "Commercial Purpose" means a purpose primarily intended to obtain
commercial advantage, revenue, monetary compensation, or another
commercial benefit.

1.11 "Non-Commercial Purpose" means a purpose that is not primarily
intended to obtain a Commercial Purpose.

1.12 "Contribution" means material intentionally submitted to the Project
for possible inclusion in the Software.

1.13 "Commercial Licensing Right" means the right granted by a
contributor under Section 10.3.

2. GRANT OF RIGHTS

Subject to the conditions of this license, each applicable Copyright
Holder grants you a worldwide, royalty-free, non-exclusive license to:

(a) use the Software for a Non-Commercial Purpose;

(b) study, inspect, and analyze the Software;

(c) modify the Software;

(d) compile the Software and Modified Software;

(e) reproduce and distribute the Software and Modified Software for a
    Non-Commercial Purpose;

(f) use the Software for artificial intelligence, machine learning, model
    training, analysis, evaluation, and research for a Non-Commercial
    Purpose; and

(g) create and distribute Programs for Koi-DOS under Section 6.

No rights are granted except those expressly stated in this license.

3. CONDITIONS FOR DISTRIBUTION

When you distribute Software or Modified Software, you must:

(a) retain applicable copyright notices;

(b) provide a copy of this license, or a stable reference to its full
    text;

(c) identify material modifications where reasonably practicable;

(d) clearly state that the distributed version has been modified; and

(e) preserve applicable notices identifying third-party material.

A modification notice may state:

"This version contains modifications by [name or project], based on
Koi-DOS [version, release, or commit]."

You are not required to publish source code for modifications that you do
not otherwise distribute.

4. NON-COMMERCIAL LIMITATION

The rights granted by Section 2 do not include use of Software or
Modified Software for a Commercial Purpose.

Without a separate written commercial license issued by the Maintainer,
you may not:

(a) sell, rent, lease, sublicense, or provide Software or Modified
    Software as a paid product or service;

(b) include Software or Modified Software in a product or service offered
    for payment;

(c) provide paid hosting, deployment, maintenance, support, consulting,
    customization, or similar services in which Software or Modified
    Software is a material component;

(d) distribute Software or Modified Software as part of a paid device,
    image, subscription, download, support plan, warranty, or service;

(e) use Software or Modified Software in the operation of a commercial
    product, service, infrastructure, or business process; or

(f) otherwise use Software or Modified Software primarily for commercial
    advantage or monetary compensation.

Free distribution by itself does not constitute a Commercial Purpose.

A person receiving a salary, scholarship, grant, or other compensation
may use the Software for personal education, study, or research without
that fact alone making the use commercial.

However, use by an employer, company, institution, or other organization
in connection with its products, services, infrastructure, or business
operations may constitute a Commercial Purpose even if the individual
user is not separately paid for that use.

A commercial license issued by the Maintainer covers material subject to
the Commercial Licensing Right. It does not cover material identified in
the LICENSE-MANIFEST as KNCL-NONCOMMERCIAL-ONLY, which requires the
separate permission of its copyright holder.

5. PERMITTED NON-COMMERCIAL USE

The following activities are permitted when they are not performed for a
Commercial Purpose:

(a) personal use, experimentation, and hobby projects;

(b) downloading, running, compiling, testing, and modifying Koi-DOS;

(c) free distribution of source code and binaries;

(d) university coursework, teaching, academic research, and study;

(e) demonstrations, reviews, benchmarks, and non-commercial videos;

(f) use by individuals, student groups, hobby groups, and non-commercial
    communities;

(g) use by public educational or research institutions; and

(h) use for artificial intelligence or machine-learning research that is
    not primarily intended to create commercial advantage or revenue.

6. PROGRAMS FOR KOI-DOS

A Program for Koi-DOS is an independent work and is not subject to KNCL
merely because it:

(a) runs on Koi-DOS;

(b) uses the Koi-DOS public ABI;

(c) calls Koi-DOS system calls;

(d) includes Interface Components;

(e) includes Redistributable SDK Components;

(f) links against a Redistributable SDK Component; or

(g) implements a documented Koi-DOS protocol or file format.

Programs for Koi-DOS may be distributed under any license chosen by their
authors, including a commercial or proprietary license, and may be sold.

Redistributable SDK Components may be compiled into a Program for
Koi-DOS and distributed as part of it, in source or binary form, under
the Program's own license. That permission covers those components as
used in a Program for Koi-DOS, and does not permit their use as a
general-purpose library outside that purpose.

This section does not permit a Program for Koi-DOS to copy, modify,
embed, link against, or distribute covered implementation code that is
not a Redistributable SDK Component.

A public header or interface definition is not an implementation license
unless the Maintainer expressly identifies it as a Redistributable SDK
Component.

7. COMBINED DISTRIBUTIONS

A distribution may contain both Koi-DOS and independent Programs for
Koi-DOS.

Such a distribution is permitted under KNCL when it is made for a
Non-Commercial Purpose.

The license of an independent Program remains separate from KNCL. KNCL
does not apply to an independent Program merely because it is distributed
in the same archive, disk image, repository, or package.

Nothing in this section grants permission to use Koi-DOS or Modified
Software for a Commercial Purpose.

8. THIRD-PARTY MATERIAL

KNCL applies only to material for which the applicable Copyright Holder
has the necessary rights and that is identified as Software under
Section 1.5.

Third-party code, libraries, fonts, artwork, assets, firmware, data,
documentation, generated material, and other components may be subject to
separate licenses.

The applicable third-party license governs each such component. Where
third-party material is present, the LICENSE-MANIFEST names the license
that applies to it.

Nothing in KNCL grants rights to third-party material beyond the rights
granted by its applicable license.

9. PROJECT NAME, TRADEMARKS, AND ENDORSEMENT

This license is a copyright license. It does not grant rights in names,
logos, or marks, which are addressed separately.

This license does not grant permission to use the names "Koi-DOS",
"Mizu", "Koi Ayame", or associated logos, artwork, or project marks to:

(a) imply endorsement, sponsorship, or approval by the Maintainer;

(b) imply that a modified version is an official release;

(c) present a modified version as an official, unmodified, or
    Maintainer-approved release; or

(d) use a Project mark as the primary branding of a modified version
    without written permission.

A distribution containing Modified Software must use a name that
distinguishes it from the official Koi-DOS project, unless the Maintainer
gives written permission otherwise.

This section does not prohibit truthful descriptive statements about
origin, compatibility, or modification, including:

"Based on Koi-DOS."

"Koi-DOS-compatible."

"Modified from Koi-DOS [version, release, or commit]."

Such statements must not imply endorsement or official status.

10. CONTRIBUTIONS

10.1 Copyright ownership

A contributor retains ownership of copyright in their Contribution.

This license does not transfer copyright ownership from a contributor to
the Maintainer or to the Project.

10.2 License to the Project

By intentionally submitting a Contribution for possible inclusion in the
Software, the contributor grants the Maintainer a perpetual, worldwide,
non-exclusive, royalty-free, irrevocable license to:

(a) reproduce the Contribution;

(b) modify, adapt, translate, rearrange, and prepare derivative works
    from the Contribution;

(c) combine the Contribution with other material;

(d) compile, execute, publicly display, and distribute the Contribution
    as part of the Software or Modified Software;

(e) maintain, reimplement, replace, or remove the Contribution;

(f) distribute the Contribution under this license, or under a later
    version of this license published by the Maintainer; and

(g) authorize recipients to exercise the rights granted by this license,
    solely in relation to the Contribution as included in the Software or
    Modified Software.

This license does not prevent the contributor from using, modifying,
distributing, or separately licensing their own Contribution, including
for a Commercial Purpose.

10.3 Commercial Licensing Right

The contributor grants the Maintainer a perpetual, worldwide,
non-exclusive, royalty-free, sublicensable license to reproduce, modify,
distribute, and authorize the commercial use of the Contribution, and to
issue, negotiate, and administer separate written commercial licenses
covering it.

This right may be exercised only for the purpose of licensing the
Software or Modified Software as a whole, or a substantial part of it,
that includes the Contribution.

It does not permit the Maintainer to license, sell, or otherwise
commercially exploit the Contribution as a standalone work, as a
general-purpose library, or as a component separated from Koi-DOS or a
work derived from Koi-DOS.

This right does not transfer ownership of copyright to the Maintainer.

The contributor is not entitled to royalties, fees, or other
compensation arising from a commercial license issued under this section
unless the contributor and the Maintainer agree otherwise in a separate
written agreement.

10.4 Scope

The rights granted by Sections 10.2 and 10.3 apply only to:

(a) the Contribution;

(b) modified versions of the Contribution; and

(c) the Contribution as combined with the Software or Modified Software.

They grant no rights in any other work owned by the contributor.

10.5 Patents

To the extent the contributor holds patent rights that would necessarily
be infringed by the Contribution as submitted, or by the Contribution as
combined with the Software, the contributor grants the Maintainer and
recipients of the Software a perpetual, worldwide, non-exclusive,
royalty-free patent license to make, use, and distribute the Contribution
as part of the Software or Modified Software.

This patent license applies only to the Contribution and its use within
the Software, and terminates for any party that initiates patent
litigation alleging that the Software infringes a patent.

10.6 Contributor representations

By submitting a Contribution, the contributor represents that:

(a) they have the legal right to submit the Contribution;

(b) they have the legal right to grant the licenses in this section, and
    that no employer, client, or other party holds rights that would
    prevent it;

(c) to the best of their knowledge, the Contribution does not knowingly
    violate the copyright, patent, trade-secret, or other rights of a
    third party; and

(d) any third-party material in the Contribution has been identified and
    accompanied by its applicable license.

10.7 No obligation to accept

The Maintainer is not required to accept, include, maintain, or
distribute any Contribution.

10.8 Contributions without the Commercial Licensing Right

A Contribution may be accepted without the Commercial Licensing Right
only if the Maintainer expressly agrees in writing.

Material accepted under such an exception must be identified in the
LICENSE-MANIFEST as KNCL-NONCOMMERCIAL-ONLY.

Software containing such material may not be distributed under a
commercial license unless the relevant copyright holder grants the
necessary additional permission.

10.9 When these terms apply

This section applies to Contributions submitted on or after the date this
version of the license was published.

A Contribution submitted earlier remains governed by the terms in effect
when it was submitted, unless its contributor agrees otherwise in
writing.

11. VERSIONS OF THIS LICENSE

The Maintainer may publish revised versions of this license. Each version
is distinguished by a version number.

Software distributed under a particular version of this license remains
available under that version. A recipient may also choose to rely on any
later version published by the Maintainer.

12. TERMINATION

The rights granted by this license terminate automatically if you
materially violate its terms.

If you receive written notice of a material violation, your rights may be
reinstated if the violation is completely cured within thirty (30) days
after receipt of the notice, unless the Maintainer agrees otherwise in
writing.

Termination does not affect rights lawfully granted to recipients before
termination, to the extent those rights cannot lawfully be revoked, and
does not affect the rights granted to the Maintainer under Section 10.

